  <prompt>
    Implement three carried-in R2 UAT round-3 polish items on the Compose editor: FR-19 (DEF-16) — the
    formatting toolbar stays pinned/sticky during scroll so it is visible at any scroll position; FR-20
    (DEF-17) — the selection bubble menu renders on a single line at default widths (no wrap to two rows);
    FR-21 (DEF-15) — the "opened with N simplification(s)" banner is dismissible via an × that closes it and
    persists dismissal for the session. All three are client-only Fluent v9 polish on the MIT TipTap base —
    NO TipTap product feature (paid or unpaid), no `@tiptap-pro/*`.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior React/TypeScript engineer fluent in TipTap 3 editor UI (bubble menu, toolbar), CSS sticky
    positioning, sessionStorage-backed UI state, and Fluent UI v9 theming (including dark mode).
  </role>

  <goal>
    Three fixes: (1) the format toolbar is `position: sticky` (or equivalent) so it remains visible while
    the document scrolls; (2) the selection bubble menu lays out on one row at default editor widths; (3)
    the simplification banner in `ComposeBannerStack.tsx` gains a dismiss × that closes it and records the
    dismissal in sessionStorage so it stays closed for the rest of the session. Matching component tests
    assert toolbar stickiness, single-line bubble layout, and dismiss-persists-for-session, plus an ADR-021
    dark-mode render check.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      These three items are R2 UAT round-3 findings (DEF-16 sticky toolbar, DEF-17 one-line bubble menu,
      DEF-15 dismissible simplification warning) explicitly carried into R3 scope per design §7.5 ("Pinned/
      sticky toolbar, one-line bubble menu | R2 UAT round-3 items (DEF-16/DEF-17) — carry in") and spec
      FR-19..21. They are client-only editor polish, independent of the E1/E2 fidelity core, and run in the
      W4 toolset parallel wave. The "opened with N simplification(s)" banner warns that the loaded doc was
      simplified on import; dismissal should persist per session so the user is not re-nagged.
    </background>
