  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare FULL rigor. Load the knowledge files + design §7.5. Read `ComposeReanchorBanner.tsx` (dismiss pattern) and `ComposeEditor.scroll.test.tsx` (scroll region).</step>
    <step order="1" name="Sticky toolbar (FR-19/DEF-16)">Make `ComposeFormatToolbar` pin/stick during scroll within the editor scroll region; verify it stays visible at any scroll position without overlapping content incorrectly.</step>
    <step order="2" name="One-line bubble menu (FR-20/DEF-17)">Adjust the bubble-menu variant so its controls lay out on a single row at default editor widths (no two-row wrap).</step>
    <step order="3" name="Dismissible simplification banner (FR-21/DEF-15)">Add an × to the "opened with N simplification(s)" banner in `ComposeBannerStack.tsx`; on dismiss, write a sessionStorage sentinel so it stays closed for the session; suppress render when the sentinel is set.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Tests">Author component tests: toolbar remains visible after scroll; bubble menu renders on one row; dismiss × hides the banner and it does not reappear when re-rendered within the session; include an ADR-021 dark-mode render check.</step>
